WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.398 --> 00:00:15.946
The next morning the earl sat in a chair by the library window.

2
00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:21.170
Cedric stood nearby, impatiently waiting for his pony to arrive.

3
00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:28.876
Peering out the open window, Cedric spotted Wilkins, the head groom, leading the pony.

4
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.561
A second groom followed with Wilkins' horse.

5
00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:36.843
"Here comes my pony!"

6
00:00:37.383 --> 00:00:38.784
Cedric shouted joyfully.

7
00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:41.865
"Oh, it's such a beautiful brown color!

8
00:00:41.885 --> 00:00:44.306
I can't wait to ride!"

9
00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:49.868
The earl almost smiled as his grandson dashed from the room.

10
00:00:49.888 --> 00:00:55.650
"That's not a small pony," the earl thought.

11
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.592
"I wonder how brave Cedric will be in the saddle."

12
00:01:02.068 --> 00:01:04.971
With the help of Wilkins, Cedric mounted his pony.

13
00:01:06.693 --> 00:01:10.357
Then Wilkins led the pony in a circle while the earl watched.

14
00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:14.701
"Am I sitting up straight, Wilkins?"

15
00:01:15.162 --> 00:01:16.042
Cedric asked.

16
00:01:16.963 --> 00:01:19.106
"The riders sit up straight at the circus."

17
00:01:20.587 --> 00:01:21.708
Wilkins smiled.

18
00:01:21.728 --> 00:01:24.992
"No one could sit up straighter, my lord."

19
00:01:27.688 --> 00:01:32.171
After a few more rounds, Wilkins and the earl were pleased with Cedric's progress.

20
00:01:33.432 --> 00:01:35.153
But Cedric wanted to do more.

21
00:01:35.173 --> 00:01:38.556
"Can I ride by myself, Grandpapa?"

22
00:01:39.036 --> 00:01:39.837
Cedric pleaded.

23
00:01:39.857 --> 00:01:42.218
"I want to go faster.

24
00:01:42.238 --> 00:01:47.322
In New York I used to see a boy trotting and galloping through the park."

25
00:01:47.342 --> 00:01:50.984
"Do you think you can handle trotting?"

26
00:01:51.465 --> 00:01:52.486
the earl asked.

27
00:01:52.506 --> 00:01:55.588
"It's not as easy as it looks."

28
00:01:57.356 --> 00:01:59.578
"I'd like to try," Cedric said.

29
00:01:59.598 --> 00:02:01.659
"All right.

30
00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.542
Wilkins, let his lordship try."

31
00:02:07.023 --> 00:02:10.085
Wilkins motioned for the other groom to bring over his horse.

32
00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:14.829
"Are you ready, your lordship?"

33
00:02:16.009 --> 00:02:17.571
Wilkins mounted his horse.

34
00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:21.053
"Ready!" Cedric shouted.

35
00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.956
The next few minutes were exciting ones for Cedric.

36
00:02:25.932 --> 00:02:29.133
He bounced in the saddle as Wilkins led his pony at a trot.

37
00:02:31.474 --> 00:02:34.495
Cedric was soon out of breath, and his face was red.

38
00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.415
But he still tried to sit up straight.

39
00:02:39.396 --> 00:02:43.017
"Trotting j-j-jolts you a g-g-good deal!"

40
00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:44.298
Cedric said.

41
00:02:44.318 --> 00:02:48.099
"You'll get used to it," Wilkins said.

42
00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:52.220
They went around a bend and disappeared from the earl's view.

43
00:02:54.864 --> 00:02:55.885
The earl chuckled.

44
00:02:55.905 --> 00:02:59.946
"I expect they'll be walking when they return."

45
00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.408
But the earl was surprised when Cedric rode into view.

46
00:03:08.748 --> 00:03:11.929
His hat was missing, and he was holding on for dear life.

47
00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.170
But he was still in the saddle, and he was still trotting.

48
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:19.071
"Stop a minute!"

49
00:03:19.451 --> 00:03:21.012
the earl called out the window.

50
00:03:23.568 --> 00:03:24.989
"Where's your hat, Cedric?"

51
00:03:25.009 --> 00:03:30.111
"It fell off, your lordship," Wilkins answered for Cedric.

52
00:03:30.131 --> 00:03:32.832
"And he wouldn't let me pick it up."

53
00:03:34.973 --> 00:03:37.034
The earl continued talking to Wilkins.

54
00:03:37.054 --> 00:03:40.335
"His lordship's not afraid, is he?"

55
00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:44.477
"I don't think he knows the meaning of the word."

56
00:03:45.517 --> 00:03:47.338
Wilkins looked proudly at his pupil.

57
00:03:47.358 --> 00:03:51.680
"I've taught many young gentlemen to ride.

58
00:03:52.604 --> 00:03:55.385
I've never had one more determined to learn."

59
00:03:56.526 --> 00:03:58.807
The earl turned his attention to his grandson.

60
00:03:58.827 --> 00:04:00.908
"Are you tired?

61
00:04:01.548 --> 00:04:02.689
Do you want to get off?"

62
00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.812
"I'm a little tired," Cedric admitted.

63
00:04:07.832 --> 00:04:10.173
"But I don't want to get down.

64
00:04:11.353 --> 00:04:14.375
As soon as I catch my breath, I'll retrieve my hat.

65
00:04:15.475 --> 00:04:16.556
Are you ready, Wilkins?"

66
00:04:19.848 --> 00:04:23.210
As they trotted away, the earl's eyes gleamed with happiness.

67
00:04:24.411 --> 00:04:26.992
He couldn't remember the last time he'd felt like this.

68
00:04:29.294 --> 00:04:32.295
A few minutes later, the two riders returned at a gallop.

69
00:04:32.315 --> 00:04:39.219
"There!" Cedric was exhausted but triumphant.

70
00:04:39.239 --> 00:04:41.041
"I galloped!

71
00:04:42.361 --> 00:04:44.523
I didn't do it as well as the boy in New York.

72
00:04:45.443 --> 00:04:46.744
But I didn't fall off!"

73
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:52.478
After that, Cedric went riding with Wilkins almost every day.

74
00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:58.261
Everyone in the countryside grew used to seeing Lord Fauntleroy on his brown pony.

75
00:05:01.202 --> 00:05:05.063
One afternoon Cedric noticed a boy limping home from the village school.

76
00:05:05.083 --> 00:05:10.546
"I'll walk, and he can ride my pony," Cedric said to Wilkins.

77
00:05:11.886 --> 00:05:15.608
Wilkins knew that a young gentleman shouldn't give up his pony for a villager.

78
00:05:17.324 --> 00:05:21.267
"No, I'll get down, and the boy can ride my horse."

79
00:05:22.748 --> 00:05:26.091
"But he might not feel comfortable on such a big animal."

80
00:05:27.011 --> 00:05:30.133
Before Wilkins could object, Cedric dismounted.

81
00:05:30.153 --> 00:05:33.476
"Besides I want to talk to him."

82
00:05:36.098 --> 00:05:39.160
The boy was too surprised to refuse Cedric's offer.

83
00:05:41.742 --> 00:05:44.644
When they reached his cottage, his mother came to the gate.

84
00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:50.647
"I've brought your son home, ma'am," Cedric said.

85
00:05:50.667 --> 00:05:53.069
"He could use some crutches.

86
00:05:54.169 --> 00:05:56.972
I'll ask my grandfather to have a pair made for him."

87
00:05:58.593 --> 00:06:02.376
Wilkins nervously watched the scene, wondering how he'd explain it.

88
00:06:02.396 --> 00:06:06.580
"The earl won't like this," he thought.

89
00:06:09.222 --> 00:06:12.164
But when the earl heard what happened, he wasn't angry.

90
00:06:13.466 --> 00:06:16.028
Instead he made Cedric tell him the story again.

91
00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:23.891
A few days later, Cedric delivered the crutches while the earl stayed in the carriage.

92
00:06:25.872 --> 00:06:29.675
When Cedric returned to the carriage, he was shaking his head in disbelief.

93
00:06:29.695 --> 00:06:34.118
"Grandpapa, it was just like when you helped Mary.

94
00:06:34.138 --> 00:06:39.241
The boy's mother was crying with happiness," he said.

95
00:06:39.261 --> 00:06:41.903
"I told her you sent the crutches.

96
00:06:43.024 --> 00:06:46.526
You didn't tell me to say that, but I thought maybe you forgot.

97
00:06:47.627 --> 00:06:48.828
That was right, wasn't it?"

98
00:06:52.799 --> 00:06:55.987
The earl laughed and didn't contradict his grandson.
